.TH DHCP-FORENSICS 8 "2026-06-02" "dhcp-oru-toolkit 2.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
dhcp-forensics \- analyze a pcap for the O-RU DHCPv4 shared-xid defect
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dhcp-forensics
.I PCAP
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.RI [ \-\-leases\ FILE ]
.RI [ \-\-config\ FILE ]
.RI [ \-\-no\-color ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dhcp-forensics
is a pure standard-library packet analyzer that reads a classic
.I pcap
or minimal
.I pcapng
capture (Ethernet / linktype 1, with 802.1Q and QinQ VLAN tags stripped),
decodes DHCPv4 and DHCPv6 messages, groups DHCPv4 messages into transactions by
their transaction id (xid), and reports findings for the Fujitsu O-RU DHCPv4
defect described in the bug report.
.PP
It does not require scapy, dpkt, tshark or tcpdump; all parsing is done with the
Python standard library only.
.PP
The analyzer detects, among others:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
shared xid across multiple units (RFC 2131 \(sc4.1);
.IP \(bu 3
units reacting to OFFERs whose chaddr is not their own (RFC 2131 \(sc4.4.1);
.IP \(bu 3
missing DHCPv4 option 61 client-identifier (RFC 4361 / O-RAN WG4 \(sc6.2.4);
.IP \(bu 3
chaddr / Ethernet-source mismatch and duplicate IP grants.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the full report as JSON instead of the rendered text report.
.TP
.B \-\-leases \fIFILE\fR
Correlate findings with an ISC/Kea lease file (cross-checks granted IPs).
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIFILE\fR
Read an ISC dhcpd.conf to map vendor classes / pools when reporting.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The capture was analyzed and no HIGH-severity findings were produced.
.TP
.B 2
At least one HIGH-severity finding was produced (for example, shared xid /
IP theft detected).
.TP
.B 1
A usage or runtime error occurred (for example, the pcap could not be read).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Analyze a capture and print the text report:
.B dhcp-forensics capture.pcap
.TP
Machine-readable output for a dashboard:
.B dhcp-forensics capture.pcap \-\-json
.TP
Analyze the synthesized O-RU reproduction fixture:
.B dhcp-forensics tests/fixtures/oru_xid_reuse.pcap
.TP
Cross-check against the server's lease database:
.B dhcp-forensics capture.pcap \-\-leases /var/lib/dhcp/dhcpd.leases
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dhcp-lease-list (8),
.BR dhcpd (8),
.BR pcap (3)
.SH AUTHOR
labuser, as part of dhcp-oru-toolkit.
